If a library isn't available, here's the minimum correct shape:

```java
public class Retry {
    private final int maxAttempts;
    private final Duration baseDelay;
    private final Duration maxDelay;
    private final Duration totalDeadline;
    private final Predicate<Throwable> retryable;
    private final Random random = new Random();

    public <T> T execute(Supplier<T> supplier) throws Exception {
        long deadline = System.nanoTime() + totalDeadline.toNanos();
        Throwable last = null;
        for (int attempt = 0; attempt < maxAttempts; attempt++) {
            try {
                return supplier.get();
            } catch (Throwable t) {
                if (!retryable.test(t)) throw asException(t);
                last = t;
                if (attempt == maxAttempts - 1) break;
                long delayMs = computeDelayMs(attempt);
                if (System.nanoTime() + millisToNanos(delayMs) > deadline) break;
                sleep(delayMs);
            }
        }
        throw asException(last);
    }

    private long computeDelayMs(int attempt) {
        long exp = (long) Math.min(
            maxDelay.toMillis(),
            baseDelay.toMillis() * (1L << attempt));   // base * 2^attempt
        return random.nextLong(exp + 1);                // FULL JITTER
    }
}
```

Notes:
- **Deadline** check before each sleep — don't sleep past the SLA.
- **Full jitter** via `random.nextLong(exp + 1)`.
- **Re-throw the last exception** if all attempts fail.
- **No swallowed errors** — caller decides what to do.
